<BaseLayout title="Privacy, credits & limits" description="How this static portfolio handles local episode files, motion preferences, external links, portrait attribution and third-party software credits."><section class="section"><div class="shell prose"><p class="eyebrow">TRANSPARENCY</p><h1>Privacy,<br/><em>credits & limits.</em></h1><h2>Local experiments</h2><p>Episode files are processed in your browser. The application does not send their contents to a server, create an account or retain them after closing the page. Downloaded files remain where you save them.</p><h2>Motion preference</h2><p>The optional key <code>id-motion</code> stores only “full” or “reduced” in this origin’s localStorage. Your system’s reduced-motion preference takes precedence. Use your browser’s site-data controls to remove it.</p><h2>Hosting and external links</h2><p>This is a static GitHub Pages site. Hosting providers may process ordinary request information under their own policies. External links open services such as GitHub, LinkedIn, ORCID and publication sources. No visitor analytics or contact-form backend is implemented here.</p><h2>Images and software</h2><p>The portrait is sourced once from the owner’s public GitHub profile and stored with the site. Some source portraits were prepared with AI assistance. Decorative diagrams are conceptual illustrations, not experimental evidence.</p><p>Astro, Quarto, GSAP and Three.js retain their respective licenses. See the repository’s third-party notices. Code access does not grant rights to reuse Isaac’s name, portrait or identity. No attached architecture books are distributed with this site.</p><h2>Scientific scope</h2><p>The agent laboratory uses a supplied map, local observations and deterministic graph search. It does not implement trained world models, continual-learning algorithms, consciousness or a robot controller.</p><a class="text-link" href="/engineering/">Version and engineering evidence ↗</a></div></section></BaseLayout>
